---
description: PayGuard Copilot project rules
alwaysApply: true
---

PROJECT: PayGuard Copilot - enterprise GenAI platform for payment disputes, fraud and compliance.

STACK: Python 3.11, FastAPI, LangChain + LangGraph, Qdrant, bge embeddings + reranker, PostgreSQL, Redis,
XGBoost + SHAP + MLflow, Presidio, RAGAS + DeepEval, Langfuse, Docker, GitHub Actions, pytest.

RULES:
1. Show a plan and wait for approval before writing code.
2. Provide complete working files, never diffs or "rest unchanged" placeholders.
3. Make minimal, targeted changes. Do not modify working modules unless the task requires it. No regressions.
4. No raw PAN/PII may reach any LLM prompt, log, vector DB or trace. Tokenize first.
5. All LLM/tool calls need timeouts, retries, structured logging and an audit-log entry.
6. SQL tool is read-only, allow-listed tables, row-limited, validated before execution.
7. Every answer carries citations (doc, section, page, effective date).
8. Config via env vars / pydantic-settings. No hardcoded secrets.
9. Every module ships with pytest tests. A phase is done only when its tests pass.
10. Type hints, docstrings, small functions. Layout: src/payguard/{gateway,rag,data,ml,agents,security,eval,platform}.
11. If ambiguous, ask one concise question instead of guessing.
12. At the end of each phase report: files created, how to run, how to test, known limitations.
13. Never invent metrics or claim a command passed unless you ran it and saw the output.
